I sit at the table again.
I take a small box.
This is my sweet for today.
"Look, this is Kozhikodan halwa," I show on the camera.
It has a nice orange color.
Then my younger sister Sofia comes in front of the camera.
There is a paper in her hand.
That is a new drawing.
A beautiful drawing with colors.
"Sofia, whose picture is that?" I ask.
"This is my drawing," Sofia says.
"This is a dog."
"Is that our Lola?" I ask.
Sofia laughs loudly.
"Yes, this is our Lola," she says.
Her drawing is very beautiful.
We are all very happy.
